{"page": 38, "text": "During the third quarter of 2026, the Company, through Elecor, sold a 49% interest in a CRE joint venture that owns a certain real estate property to an unrelated third party. Elecor will continue to manage the property. The Company deconsolidated the CRE joint venture and recognized its retained interest at fair value, determined based on the transaction price plus capitalized transaction costs. The retained interest is accounted for under the equity method and is presented within other assets on the consolidated balance sheets. The Company recognized a $26.8 million gain on sale, including a gain attributable to remeasurement of the retained interest to fair value, within realized and unrealized gains (losses), net on the consolidated statements of operations. Following the transaction, the CRE joint venture is a related party of the Company.\nThe Company leases office, retail and storage space to tenants, primarily under non-cancellable operating leases which generally have terms ranging from five to fifteen years. Most of the Company\u2019s leases provide tenants with extension options at either fixed or market rates. Certain leases provide tenants with options to terminate early, but such options generally impose an economic penalty on the tenant upon exercising.\nThe following table summarizes rental revenue and other variable revenue based on the specific lease terms presented in commercial real estate revenue on the consolidated statements of operations for the period:\nThree Months Ended September 30, Nine Months Ended September 30,\n2026 2025 2026 2025\nRental revenue $ 150,704 $ \u2014 $ 459,964 $ \u2014\nOther variable revenue 36,337 \u2014 87,464 \u2014\nTotal $ 187,041 $ \u2014 $ 547,428 $ \u2014\n30\nRITHM CAPITAL CORP. AND SUBSIDIARIES\nNOTES TO CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS (UNAUDITED)\n(dollars in tables in thousands, except share and per share data)\nThe following table summarizes the future minimum rental revenue under e