{"page": 156, "text": "Interest income was $479.6 million for the three months ended September 30, 2026, an increase of $5.0 million, compared to $474.6 million for the three months ended June 30, 2026. The increase was primarily attributable to higher interest income from (i) our Origination and Servicing business, driven by a higher custodial earnings rate, and (ii) our Asset Management business driven by higher interest earned from insurance company investments. The increase was partially offset by lower interest income from on-balance sheet Non-QM and consumer loans due to securitizations during the three months ended September 30, 2026.\nNine months ended September 30, 2026 compared to the nine months ended September 30, 2025\nInterest income was $1,416.1 million for the nine months ended September 30, 2026, an increase of $42.6 million, compared to $1,373.5 million for the nine months ended September 30, 2025. The increase was primarily attributable to (i) growth in the Non-QM, RTL and consumer portfolios, and (ii) nine months of interest income earned from insurance company investments acquired in December 2025, as compared to none in the prior year period. The increase was partially offset by net securities sales, securitizations and a loweir average earnings rate on custodial balances in Origination and Servicing. 118\nGain on Originated Residential Mortgage Loans, HFS, Net\nThe following table provides information regarding gain on originated residential mortgage loans, HFS, net as a percentage of pull through adjusted lock volume, by channel:\nThree Months Ended Nine Months Ended September 30,\n(dollars in thousands) September 30,\n2026 June 30,\n2026 2026 2025 QoQ Change YoY Change\nGain on originated residential mortgage loans, held-for-sale, net(A)(B)(C)(D) $ 177,390 $ 184,323 $ 546,810 $ 501,724 $ (6,933) $ 45,086\nPull through adjusted lock volume $ 12,418,341 $ 14,493,879 $ 43,871,237 $ 46,785,204 $ (2,075,538) $ (2,913,967)\nGain on Originated Resi