 months ended September 30, 2026, a decrease of $28.1 million, compared to $410.5 million for the three months ended June 30, 2026. The decrease was primarily due to (i) decreased performance-based compensation and (ii) lower commissions in Origination and Servicing during the three months ended September 30, 2026.\nNine months ended September 30, 2026 compared to the nine months ended September 30, 2025\nCompensation and benefits expenses were $1.2 billion for the nine months ended September 30, 2026, an increase of $306.3 million, compared to $864.9 million for the nine months ended September 30, 2025. The increase was primarily attributable to increased headcount following the acquisitions of Elecor and Crestline in December 2025, reflecting nine months of expenses in the current period compared to none in the prior year period.\nDepreciation and Amortization\nThe following table includes the breakdown of depreciation and amortization expense by segment for the periods presented:\n"}
